# SEO & Routing Rules

## Page Structure
- Exactly **one H1** per page — real text, never in an image or canvas
- Use Next.js Metadata API for `<title>`, `<meta description>`, canonical
- Include JSON-LD schema (Organization on layouts, WebPage on pages)
- Semantic HTML hierarchy: h1 → h2 → h3, no skipping levels

## Internationalization
- Spanish: `/` (default, x-default)
- English: `/en/`
- Every page needs `hreflang` alternates for both locales
- Set `<html lang="es">` or `<html lang="en">` per locale
- Use `generatePageMetadata()` from `src/lib/metadata.ts`

## Server Rendering
- Pages must be server-rendered, not client-only JS
- Keep content in page components, not loaded via client fetch
- Static generation preferred where possible

## Files
- `sitemap.xml` at `/sitemap.xml` (generated by `src/app/sitemap.ts`)
- `robots.txt` at `/robots.txt` (in `public/`)
- Open Graph image at `/og-image.jpg`

## Legacy Folder
The `legacy/` folder contains the old static site. It is:
- **Never served in production** (outside Next.js app/public)
- Excluded from builds via `.vercelignore`
- Blocked by robots.txt: `Disallow: /legacy/`
- Preserved only for reference — do not modify or deploy

## Internal Routes
- `/sistema` is noindex (design system showcase for internal review)
- Add `robots: { index: false, follow: false }` to any internal-only pages
